# Command atop

## What does this command do:

System and process monitor for Linux

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: sudo dnf install -y atop

## Command path

For Fedora run: /usr/sbin/atop

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://packages.fedoraproject.org/pkgs/atop/atop/

## Command options

# Live monitoring (interactive)
atop
atop 5              # refresh every 5 seconds
atop -a             # show all processes/cgroups, not just active

# Sort processes by resource
atop -C             # sort by CPU (default)
atop -M             # sort by memory
atop -D             # sort by disk activity
atop -N             # sort by network activity

# Alternate process views (press these keys interactively too)
atop -m             # memory-related process info
atop -d             # disk-related process info
atop -n             # network-related process info
atop -s             # scheduling-related process info
atop -c             # show command line per process

# Bar graphs
atop -B             # bar graphs for system statistics

# Record and replay
atop -w /var/log/atop/atop.raw 60      # write raw samples every 60s
atop -r /var/log/atop/atop.raw          # replay a raw logfile
atop -r y -b 1400 -e 1600               # replay yesterday, 14:00-16:00

# Version info
atop -V
